<title>USA: Cyclone drifting south in Mozambique Channel.</title>
<headline>Cyclone drifting south in Mozambique Channel.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Giuette is drifting southward in the Mozambique Channel, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Friday.</p>
<p>The cyclone, with 50 mph winds, is near 22s/40e, between Madagascar and Mozambique, moving south at five mph.</p>
<p>This motion was expected to continue as the storm slowly strengthened during the next 24 hours, threatening mostly shipping, WSC said.</p>
